<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| cross-tree `form=` association | a control outside the form element commits through it, exercising the delegated-listener path |
| planning record → future readers | the ledger is the artifact a future phase will trust about what is and is not fixed |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-28-07-A | Repudiation | a ledger that overstates coverage, leaving a live defect recorded as closed | mitigate | per-clause evidence against each requirement's own wording, checks cited by name, the CFG-65 precedent for honest non-closure, and a grep enforcing the overclaim ban across the planning tree |
| T-28-07-B | Tampering | a check count taken from arithmetic drifting from reality | mitigate | every total re-derived by running, with the producing command recorded beside it |
| T-28-07-C | Spoofing | a runway check that passes because the control was quietly nested rather than because the `form=` path works | mitigate | the association clause asserts `form.contains(radio) === false`, and M-B mutates the delegated listener to prove the check sees that regression |
| T-28-07-D | Information Disclosure | a toast reachability check that passes on an invisible toast | mitigate | resolved opacity, viewport containment, `elementFromPoint` and the transformed-ancestor walk — four independent clauses, with M-B recording whether presence-only would have passed |
| T-28-07-SC | Tampering | npm/pip/cargo installs | n/a | zero packages installed; this plan writes no application code and adds no dependency |
</threat_model>

